+## What If It Still Failed?
+
+### Scenario: Fix Didn't Work
+
+If verify_solution still reported failures:
+
+```
+SAMPLES: FAIL (sample_1.txt: expected '5', got '20')
+```
+
+This would mean the fix wasn't actually applied or was incorrect.
+
+**Agent would:**
+1. Check why min() still failed (impossible unless Python min() is broken)
+2. Examine the actual code file
+3. Verify the edit was saved
+4. Try again
+
+This would loop back to Step 1 of Round 3 with new analysis.
+
+### Scenario: Complexity Issue (Hypothetical)
+
+If the solution was more complex and reported:
+
+```
+SAMPLES: PASS
+RANDOM: PASS
+MAX: TLE (7.1s)
+```
+
+**Agent would:**
+1. Identify: Algorithm is O(N^2) or slower for N=100,000
+2. Redesign: Change to O(N) or O(N log N) algorithm
+3. Update notes.md with new algorithm
+4. Implement new solution
+5. Re-verify (back to Step 3)
+
+This would loop through Round 3 multiple times until all gates pass.
