+## Common Fixes Cheat Sheet
+
+### Fix 1: Wrong Function
+```python
+# Problem: Using wrong built-in function
+# BEFORE
+result = max(arr)  # or .sort(), or reverse()
+
+# AFTER
+result = min(arr)  # or sorted(), or arr[::-1]
+```
+
+### Fix 2: Off-by-One Error
+```python
+# Problem: Loop range is off
+# BEFORE
+for i in range(n-1):  # Misses last element!
+
+# AFTER
+for i in range(n):  # Correct: 0 to n-1
+```
+
+### Fix 3: Duplicate Handling
+```python
+# Problem: Not accounting for duplicates
+# BEFORE
+if x == target - x:
+    result += 1  # Wrong for duplicates!
+
+# AFTER
+if x == target - x and x in seen:
+    result += seen[x] - 1  # Subtract 1 for current
+```
+
+### Fix 4: Inefficient Algorithm
+```python
+# Problem: O(N²) for large N
+# BEFORE (TLE)
+for i in range(n):
+    for j in range(n):
+        if arr[i] == arr[j]:  # O(N²)
+            ...
+
+# AFTER (Pass)
+seen = set(arr)  # O(N)
+for x in seen:
+    ...  # Use set membership: O(1)
+```
+
+### Fix 5: Integer Overflow (Python specific)
+```python
+# In Python, this is usually not an issue
+# But for other languages or very large numbers:
+
+# BEFORE (if using 32-bit math)
+result = a + b  # Might overflow
+
+# AFTER (use bigger type or Python's unlimited int)
+result = int(a) + int(b)  # Python handles automatically
+```
+
