+## Golden Rules for Round 3
+
+1. **Always run verify_solution after every code change**
+   - This is your objective signal
+   - Don't trust manual testing alone
+
+2. **Document every diagnosis in notes.md**
+   - Help yourself understand what went wrong
+   - Help reviewers understand the fix
+
+3. **Never skip complexity analysis**
+   - Before implementing, estimate time for N=10^5
+   - Will O(N) = 100,000 ops fit?
+   - Will O(N log N) = 1,000,000 ops fit?
+   - Will O(N²) = 10,000,000,000 ops FAIL?
+
+4. **Prefer algorithm change over micro-optimizations**
+   - If TLE, change from O(N²) to O(N log N)
+   - Don't try to squeeze 10% speed improvement
+   - Algorithmic improvements give 100x+ speedup
+
+5. **Test the exact scenario that failed**
+   - For SAMPLES fail: manually run that sample
+   - For RANDOM fail: regenerate that seed
+   - For MAX fail: time that exact input
+
+6. **Don't give up before Round 3 ends**
+   - You get multiple attempts per round
+   - Fix, verify, repeat is the standard process
+   - Only give up after 5 rounds
+
